omx-plugins (0.19.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: build the RPMs for fedora 45 again
  * Ceilings follow the channel: omx-clap-core < 0.31, plugin-hostd < 0.20
  * changelog: omx-doubler, omx-tone and omx-ducker are new in 0.19.0
  * githooks: commit-msg is the shared v1 stub
  * docs: the parameter pages of omx doubler, omx tone and omx ducker
  * docs: omx doubler, omx tone and omx ducker in the catalogue
  * omx doubler, omx tone and omx ducker: the kernel-identity tests
  * packaging: omx doubler, omx tone and omx ducker in the packages, with
    factory presets
  * omx doubler, omx tone and omx ducker: CLAP and LV2 faces in plain C over
    omx-dsp's doubler, tone and comp faces
  * omx doubler, omx tone and omx ducker: the generated parameter headers,
    LV2 descriptions and MOD GUIs
  * omx doubler, omx tone and omx ducker: their declarations
  * The wizard binds a single face's fixed and held controls as gen.mjs does
  * param-contract-abi: hold the row to omx-clap-core's entry, not to a type
    this tree dropped
  * round trip: name the choice control the merge left out of LOSSES
  * release: keep channel-deps on the DEB call
  * release: fedora-versions belongs to the rpm call only
  * release: build the RPMs for fedora 44 only
  * omx-plugins: .githooks/commit-msg is the shared stub of FreeMixer/.github
    v1
  * The strip tests find the tree without import.meta.dirname
  * wave-deps names only the siblings that have a dedupe/all
  * Every dependency on a library of ours states a floor and a ceiling
  * The strip tests find the tree without import.meta.dirname
  * The shared checks run from FreeMixer/.github, and clap-validator is
    required
  * wave-deps names only the siblings that have a dedupe/all
  * placement: a declaration's strips is a restriction, not the console's rack
  * release: omx-plugins 0.19.0, on omx-dsp 0.30.0, omx-contract 3.9.0 and
    omx-panel 0.10.0
  * No tracked file points into a private repository, by the shared check
  * descriptor: the feature words are read from omx-contract's schema
  * ci: a pull request into dedupe/all builds on its siblings' dedupe/all
  * panel: the description header's enums are held to the declared words
  * contract: the param-contract ABI is read from omx-clap-core's header
  * faces: a meter's LV2 port is structural, fixed before the audio and the
    parameters
  * oracles: the dynamic EQ's and the multiband's readouts against the audio
  * faces: meters on the LV2 face and in the descriptor
  * ci: a pull request into dedupe/all builds on its siblings' dedupe/all
  * omx-strip: the CLAP remote-control pages follow Bands
  * omx-strip: a band's controls are shown while Bands reaches it
  * meter-level: compare the level readings within omx-dsp's fast-maths bound
  * faces: the host's bypass keeps one CLAP id, and LV2 enabled and latency
    one port each
  * packaging: the Debian .docs and .install lists carry the licence lines
  * omx-glue: Detector Topology reads comp's DETECTOR_TOPOLOGY, one
    declaration
  * omx-strip: the band count against the strip before it, and its CPU cost
  * omx-strip: an EQ of up to 32 bands, chosen by a Bands control (#308)
  * gen: a chain element's band count and its appended parameters
  * omx-delay: tempo sync, division, mode and duck (FX-4)
  * faces: the host's tempo reaches a plugin that reads one
  * docs: omx-glue's parameter reference carries Detector Topology (make
    params-doc)
  * presets: ssl-bus-glue runs the feedback detector; omx-glue gains VCA Bus
    4:1
  * omx-glue: Detector Topology, appended at id 7, default Feedforward
  * comp: the ducker preset, ratio 20 held at a -12 dB range
  * omx-limiter: latency checks hold the reported look-ahead to the impulse
  * packaging: every package installs its licence and the short README
  * make panel-copies: no tracked file is a film strip or a fixture omx-panel
    ships
  * modgui: the film strips come from omx-panel at build time, none committed
  * packaging: no markdown in the packages; their descriptions name
    openmixer.org

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:39:39 +0000
